helper.BatchIntro:
Take-profit and stop-loss in batches: 
The positions being followed can be sold in batches, and multiple take-profit/stop-loss rules can be configured; 
when the stop-profit and stop-loss is triggered, N% of the currently followed position will be sold (triggered from the 1st level); 
the stop-profit/stop-loss is only triggered once for each level of the same token; 
if the same token is added to the position, the take-profit/stop-loss will be re-run at the average price (triggered from the 1st level again)

helper.BuySettingsIntro1:
Maximum follow-up purchase: 

Maximum follow-up purchase means that the user is willing to use up to N SOL as the copy order amount; 
if the purchase amount of the target address > the maximum purchase amount, the purchase amount will be the maximum purchase amount; 
if the purchase amount of the target address = < the maximum purchase amount, the copy purchase will be based on the purchase amount of the target address. 

Example: If the user sets a maximum buy-in of 10 SOL. 
If the copy address buys 5 SOL, the user will follow the order and buy 5 SOL; 
If the target copy address buys 20 SOL, the user will follow the order and buy 10 SOL.

helper.PlatformIntro:
Only when the token purchased by the copy wallet is the token of the selected platform, will it copy the purchase (it does not affect the copy selling).
For example, if token A is created in Pump, the user only sets the Pump platform.
When the copy target wallet buys A in the Pump internal market, it can copy the purchase;
After the liquidity of A is migrated to Raydium, the copy target wallet buys A again and no longer copy the purchase; the user sells A on Raydium and can copy the sale;
If the user adjusts the copy platform to: Pump + Raydium; when the copy target wallet buys again on Raydium, it can copy the purchase;

